<PageLayout title="Pricing — TotalRecalls" description="One-time $24 launch price. No subscription. A free web tier is coming soon." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Pricing" }]}>

  <h1>Pricing</h1>
  <p>TotalRecalls is a small Windows app that downloads and saves your ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen conversations into a private folder on your computer — readable Markdown + JSON you keep forever.</p>
  <p>No subscription. No cloud locker. No account required.</p>

  <section class="price-card">
    <h2>Launch Price</h2>
    <div class="price-block">
      <span class="price-current" data-tr-price>$24</span>
      <span class="price-badge">launch price</span>
    </div>
    <p class="price-note">One-time purchase · Windows app · Local files only</p>
    <p>Pay once with Lemon Squeezy. You'll receive a download link for the Windows app immediately after purchase.</p>
    <a href="https://totalrecalls.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/buy/03e11a51-8c63-4826-8b87-998b626285c3" data-tr-buy class="buy-button buy-lg">Buy TotalRecalls — <span data-tr-price>$24</span></a>
    <p class="guarantee-note">A free web tier is on the way — a browser app you can run on your own chats before paying a cent, which is our replacement for money-back refunds.</p>
    <p class="early-access-note">Early access build. Actively improving based on user feedback.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What You Get</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Export from ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini (Takeout), Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen</li>
      <li>Local Markdown + JSON files</li>
      <li>Private folder structure you own</li>
      <li>No cloud storage</li>
      <li>No telemetry</li>
      <li>No recurring fees</li>
      <li>Free minor updates during the launch period</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why $24?</h2>
    <p>Launch price — $24 one-time, no subscription. Every conversation, one library, yours forever.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No Refund Policy — By Design</h2>
    <p>We don't offer a 14-day money-back guarantee. Instead, we're shipping a <strong>free web tier</strong>: you'll be able to try the full export on your own chats before paying anything. If the free tier isn't for you, you've lost nothing — which is the point.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why One-Time Pricing?</h2>
    <p>TotalRecalls is a utility, not a subscription service. You pay once, download the app, and keep your archive forever.</p>
    <p>Later, when advanced features arrive (semantic search, Obsidian/Notion sync, RAG containers, multi-device memory), those will be <strong>optional upgrades</strong> — not required for basic exporting.</p>
  </section>

